# EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR: bad_interp_format_wrapper.obs:(15,23): Cannot apply format specifier '.2' to expression: 'args'
# EXPECT_ERROR_COUNT: 1
#~
A format that does not fit the value is one error, at the interpolation, in the program's own
words. The format is applied by a call the compiler writes around the expression
('Float->ToString((args)->As(Float), 2)' for "{$args:.2}"), and what the analyzer said about that
call was passed on as it came: "Dimension size mismatch" and "Invalid array cast", at line 1 of
the file and at columns counted in the compiler's text, which for a longer expression was quoted
back as well.
~#
class BadInterpFormatWrapper {
	function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
		ratio := 0.5;
		ok := "ratio {$ratio:.2}";
		bad := "arguments {$args:.2}";
		ok->PrintLine();
		bad->PrintLine();
	}
}
